{"title":"2007 BMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Bulgaria</i>)\nFind all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc081f5ac7df268e035e0f6a94f4d83b73724b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f : \\mathbb{R} \\mapsto \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc5e9d1d4b6e5060195e858ce2f2b2944e2efaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(f(x) + y) = f(f(x) - y) + 4f(x)y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56df81157e7052306c4785297ad7e2c80a012c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c1a57575c7b42074f8e0a2992f77fb97aa8732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> is a solution to the equation.  Henceforth we shall consider other solutions to the equations, i.e., functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228663427166fa0dd8911ea5e0d4c3ddfd5ded79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> such that for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be9c3d50f54aca031d819fbe4d05ca6feeac5106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle c$\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1c87a812e7d8d39e7d5ceb2c06cfa0bc27b4a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(c) \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/828e4c1d20eecffaa8492747b63a6460ec659d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y = f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/79276cd7839254f45848d9c91faf7cc8770bb22a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(2f(x)) = f(0) + [f(x)]^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We note that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5a07f2a22fcb2626031da734012c71b549782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/b/2ab378c1f6bfe1433b4b57b41e6d7112d112fbc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f \\left[ f(c) + \\frac{x}{4f(c)} \\right] - f \\left[ f(c) - \\frac{x}{4f(c)} \\right] = f(c)\\cdot \\frac{x}{4f(c)} = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"442\" height=\"45\" />, i.e., as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526bd77b4de5c74c1a40d9bb93c66189acdebf36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle a$\" width=\"9\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d9743ceabd07de72ebffcaa9730cfbe1226c541e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle b$\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" /> assume all real values, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/560cef9062dfe181bb67a87c378a2be5df31581c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(b) - f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> assume all real values.\n</p><p>Now, setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb9ef72c8c22d0cf08f46dbc9446ffceea825c93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a65210ad27721ffd4a21e103fd2c6ffbd16634f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y = 2f(a) - f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />, we obtain\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e65de59c572b0a4bde0f2d0a95a0f444948496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f[2f(a)] = f\\{ 2[f(b)-f(a)]\\} + 4f(b)[2f(a)-f(b)]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"19\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>or\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4831746a070c5c94d835181ee28517e979dfb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f\\{ 2[f(b) - f(a)]\\} = 4[f(a)]^2 +f(0) - 8f(a)f(b) + 4[f(b)]^2 + f(0) = \\{ 2[f(b) - f(a)] \\}^2 + f(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"729\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/2170b18761b49cf14f424ce77708dbf2ffa3bd59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 2[ f(b) - f(a) ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> takes on all real values, it follows that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5a07f2a22fcb2626031da734012c71b549782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6efcd88a4e88079df275b806ec9af84c4639a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(x) = x^2 + f(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" />.  It is easy to see that any value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fe30b7ea04282a3f0548e9811d944139e6765cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> will satisfy the desired condition.  Thus the only solutions to the functional equation are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c1a57575c7b42074f8e0a2992f77fb97aa8732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63ccd7e28698d65478e5c709ade1c971e9f7ae6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f(x) = x^2 + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be9c3d50f54aca031d819fbe4d05ca6feeac5106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle c$\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" /> an arbitrary constant.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_BMO_Problems\" title=\"2007 BMO Problems\">2007 BMO Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=827178#827178\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213645\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 140/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 344/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4888/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.731      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.731      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4915:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213645 and revision id 14823. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}